    The Diversified Program was conceived, tested, and refined by Douglas Bry
and Philip Spertus. The approach is fully computerized and nondiscretionary.
Money management principles are a critical element in the Diversified Program
and have been carefully constructed and are rigorously applied to minimize risk
exposure and to protect asset appreciation. Since the trading methods to be
utilized by Northfield in the Diversified Program are proprietary and
confidential, the discussion that follows is of a general nature and is not
intended to be exhaustive.


