Therefore, market exposure to profitable positions is not changed based on the
time horizon of the trade; positions held for two to four months are not
unusual, and positions have been held for more than one year. Losing positions
are generally pared relatively quickly, with most closing within a few days or
weeks. However, if the JWH system detects a profitable underlying trend, a
position trading at a loss may be retained in order to capture the potential
benefits of participating in that trend. Throughout the investment process, risk
controls designed to reduce the possibility of an extraordinary loss in any one
market are maintained.

